  "slug": "adna-alignment-sensitivity-dbd7",
  "summary": "Seed-based tools are being redesigned for speed and damage tolerance across ancient DNA, genome similarity, and CRISPR off-target search.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is seeding and hashing strategies that cut the cost of sequence comparison. Hybrid RY-mers add damage-aware multi-context seeds to strobealign, improving aDNA read alignment accuracy and running 4-6x faster than BWA-aln. TurboANI applies SIMD seeding and bitset minwise hashing to homology-aware average nucleotide identity estimation, reporting up to ~40,000-fold speedup. AutoFFinder moves multi-guide CRISPR/Cas9 off-target search onto a runtime-reconfigurable FPGA platform on hg38, reported faster than GPU and CPU baselines. What is new in each case is a seed or hardware design matched to a specific bottleneck, rather than a general acceleration claim.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-12"
}
